From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:29:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gunyah: share prepared boot RAM and DRM pool

Port the fixed host DRM arena from Droid-VM 20f1e3a2, dc7388af and
93e158d2. Carve the pool from requested RAM and retain its firmware
and renderer ABI. Prepare boot mappings as 2 MiB folios, transfer
the boot window's lock charge to VM-fd SHARE, and report terminal
shim admission failures to the run loop.

Keep the existing VM-fd runtime SHARE implementation and Linux
memory policy. Only the single preparation mode and fixed DRM
pool used by the shared-memory desktop profiles are included.

BUG=None
TEST=ARM64 release build; Linux and shared-memory argument matrices
TEST=shim failure notification unit test

Purpose: Share prepared boot RAM and DRM pool.
Origin: Droid-VM/crosvm commits cited above.
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
